Drove efficiency across Citi’s container base-image ecosystem through adoption of RHEL 9 UBI Minimal/Micro, multi-stage builds, Java runtime optimisation using jlink, automated dependency updates and release-on-demand capabilities. Achieved runtime image-size reductions of up to 60% across applicable workloads within 14+ image families, including Java, Apache, NGINX, NodeJS and Python etc.. Improved the cadence of approved runtime-image delivery, reducing recurring maintenance effort and image storage and distribution overhead while enabling development teams to consume updated, optimised images more efficiently.
Responded to senior leadership escalation to support the strategically important Digital Custody / EarlyLight initiative and its critical delivery commitment. Helped address material technical dependencies arising from manual, error-prone vendor-image ingestion and the absence of an established s390x base image, image-building capability and scanning approach. Partnered across teams to progress an enterprise-supported RHEL 9 UBI s390x image and associated build and scanning capabilities, helping establish a viable delivery path and reusable technical foundations for this business-critical initiative.
