Strengthened the resilience of Vulnerability Scanning as a Service by removing a critical single-console dependency and enabling Active-Active operation across multiple Aqua SaaS instances. Improved health-check efficiency and reporting responsiveness for a service handling more than 300,000 image scans per month. These architectural and operational improvements enhanced availability, scalability and service continuity while supporting zero-downtime deployment capabilities.
Stepped in following Jon Meadows’ escalation to help progress the strategically important Digital Asset Custody programme towards production. Partnered with Digital Custody and Mainframe Engineering teams to address critical architecture, security and delivery challenges for IBM workloads outside Citi’s standard container platform and existing Lightspeed Enterprise capabilities. Provided technical leadership across architecture and security reviews, vendor-image onboarding and supply-chain controls, helping establish an alternative ingestion approach where the standard 3PiiP registry-based process was not applicable. Supported delivery of an enterprise-supported RHEL 9 UBI image for IBM/LinuxONE s390x workloads, together with a dedicated build and scanning capability. 
Demonstrated decisive ownership following an escalation from Jon Meadows. Delivered container image inventories and supporting Artifactory information for 36 in-scope applications under tight deadlines, including out-of-hours support during the migration window. Worked with programme, infrastructure and security stakeholders to improve visibility of image-retention and availability risks, informing time-critical leadership decisions, mitigation planning and recovery preparedness for critical US business services.
Led the migration of OpenShift operator and platform image ingestion from a manual, error-prone process to Citi’s standardised Third-Party Image Ingestion Pipeline (3PiiP). Partnered with OpenShift Platform and Artifactory Engineering and Operations to implement the required controls, address digest-based image references and establish a consistent, traceable and scalable ingestion process. The pipeline has supported more than 3,000 executions to ingest platform and operator images, strengthening supply-chain governance, improving consistency and remove reliance on manual handling of promotion.




